.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rcmake
is a native replacement for CMake 4.5.1 written from scratch in safe Rust.
One multi-call binary provides
.BR cmake ,
.BR ccmake
on Unix,
.BR ctest ,
.BR cpack ,
and the Language Server Protocol server, which starts through the
.B rcmake-lsp
symlink or as
.BR "rcmake lsp" .
An isolated sibling companion binary,
.BR rcmake-verify ,
handles explicit oracle comparisons for
.BR "rcmake verify" .
It reads the same
.IR CMakeLists.txt ,
presets, and
.I CMakeCache.txt
files as CMake 4.5.1, writes compatible build trees, and supports C, C++,
Objective-C, Objective-C++, Fortran, CUDA (NVCC and Clang, including separable
compilation and device linking), HIP (AMD ROCm, SPIR-V, and NVIDIA), Swift
(including split compilation under
.BR CMP0157 ,
.BR CMP0195 ,
.BR CMP0215 ,
and
.BR CMP0216 ),
C++20 named modules with Ninja dynamic dependencies, and Qt AUTOGEN.
.SS Execution modes
The executable selects its command-line mode from
.BR argv[0] .
.TP
.B Native mode (\fBrcmake\fP)
Enables the persistent compiler probe cache, sound incremental configure replay
(including toolchains, configure presets,
.B \-C
scripts, and
.IR PreLoad.cmake ),
the native subcommands
.RB ( explain ,
.BR diff-config ,
.BR fmt ,
.BR lint ,
.BR verify ,
.BR doctor ,
.BR cache ),
rich diagnostics, configure profiling, hermetic input checks, FetchContent
lockfile enforcement, stale
.I CMakeCache.txt
drift tracking, and multi-configuration
.I compile_commands.json
export.
Build-time regenerations of a build tree configured in native mode keep the
native persona.
.TP
.B Compatibility mode (\fBcmake\fP, \fBccmake\fP, \fBctest\fP, \fBcpack\fP)
Matches CMake 4.5.1 command-line flags, diagnostic formatting, and exit codes.
Compatibility mode rejects native extension flags as unknown options and writes
no native metadata files.
Setting
.B RCMAKE_ORACLE_MODE=1
forces compatibility mode even when invoked as
.BR rcmake .
.SH NATIVE EXTENSIONS
These subcommands and flags work only in native
.B rcmake
mode, and compatibility mode rejects them.
Configure-only flags such as
.BR \-\-profile ,
.BR \-\-hermetic ,
.BR \-\-fetch-lock ,
.BR \-\-no-probe-cache ,
and
.B \-\-export-compile-commands
apply during project configure.
The
.B \-\-diagnostics=cmake|rich
flag and default terminal rich errors also apply in native
.B rcmake \-P
script mode.
Compatibility
.B cmake \-P
always uses CMake diagnostic format.
.SS Explain subcommand
.B rcmake explain
evaluates the project in memory over the configured build directory without
running external processes or writing to disk.
.TP
.BI "rcmake explain " name
Inspect a configured build directory and explain where target
.I name
gets its compile flags, definitions, include directories, and link libraries,
or where variable
.I name
gets its effective value and cache provenance.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-B " build-dir"
Read
.I CMakeCache.txt
from
.IR build-dir .
The default is the current working directory.
.TP
.B \-\-target
Look up a target or alias.
.TP
.B \-\-var
Look up a variable.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-target ,
.BR \-\-config ,
and the entry filter options.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " cfg"
Select a target build configuration such as
.B Debug
or
.BR Release .
Implies
.B \-\-target
and scopes
.B \-\-dep
paths to that configuration.
.TP
.BI \-\-filter " val"
Select an exact matching target value or compiler flag such as
.B \-O2
or
.BR \-DFOO=1 .
Implies
.BR \-\-target .
.TP
.BI \-\-flag " flag"
Show where a compile or link flag comes from.
Implies
.BR \-\-target .
Use
.BI \-\-flag= flag
when the flag starts with
.BR \-\- .
.TP
.BI \-\-define " name"
Show where a preprocessor definition comes from, matching
.I NAME
or
.IR NAME=VALUE .
Implies
.BR \-\-target .
.TP
.BI \-\-include " dir"
Show where an include directory comes from.
Implies
.BR \-\-target .
.TP
.BI \-\-dep " target"
Show link and order-only dependency paths from the queried target to
.IR target .
The search stops at 16 paths, depth 32, or 20,000 edges and reports when the
result is incomplete.
Implies
.BR \-\-target .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit one JSON report in the
.B rcmake-explain-v1
format to standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show full values and call stacks in terminal output.
.TP
.BR \-\-color=auto | always | never
Control ANSI color output.
The default is
.BR auto .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show
.B rcmake explain
usage and exit.
Use with
.B \-\-find
or
.B \-\-eval
to show mode-specific help.
.PP
The filter options
.BR \-\-filter ,
.BR \-\-flag ,
.BR \-\-define ,
.BR \-\-include ,
and
.B \-\-dep
exclude each other.
.RE
.TP
.BI "rcmake explain \-\-find " pkg "\fR, \fPrcmake explain why-not " pkg
Explain how
.B find_package()
searched for
.I pkg
and why candidates were accepted or rejected.
Reads the saved native trace in
.I CMakeFiles/rcmake/find-trace.v1.json
when current, and otherwise evaluates the project again in memory.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-B " build-dir"
Read the configured build directory.
The default is the current working directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-call " n"
Select call number
.I n
(1-based) when the project calls
.B find_package()
for
.I pkg
more than once.
.TP
.B \-\-all-candidates
Show every tested path instead of only rejected files.
.TP
.B \-\-fresh
Ignore any saved trace and re-evaluate the search.
.TP
.BR \-\-json ", " \-\-color=auto | always | never
Emit JSON or control terminal color.
.RE
.TP
.BI "rcmake explain \-\-eval " expr "\fR, \fPrcmake explain " target " \-\-eval-property " prop
Evaluate a generator expression or target property in the context of a
configured build directory and show the evaluation steps.
Put
.I expr
in single quotes so the shell does not expand
.BR $< ,
or pass
.BI @ file
to read up to 64 KiB from a file.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-B " build-dir"
Read the configured build directory.
The default is the current working directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-target " name"
Evaluate as consuming target
.IR name .
With
.BR \-\-eval-property ,
the positional target is the property owner and the default consumer is the
same target.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " cfg"
Evaluate only for configuration
.IR cfg .
The default evaluates every configured build type.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " lang"
Set
.BR $<COMPILE_LANGUAGE> .
.TP
.BI \-\-link-lang " lang"
Set
.BR $<LINK_LANGUAGE> .
.TP
.BI \-\-directory " dir"
Look up target names from source directory
.IR dir .
.TP
.B \-\-link
Follow link-only usage
.RB ( $<LINK_ONLY:...> ).
.TP
.BI \-\-command-config " cfg"
Set
.B $<COMMAND_CONFIG>
for cross-configuration evaluation.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-config " cfg"
Set
.B $<OUTPUT_CONFIG>
for cross-configuration evaluation.
.TP
.B \-\-no-steps
Print only the evaluated result without intermediate steps.
.TP
.BR \-\-json ", " \-\-color=auto | always | never
Emit JSON or control terminal color.
.RE
.SS Diff-config subcommand
.TP
.BI "rcmake diff-config " dirA " " dirB
Compare two configured build directories produced by either
.B cmake
or
.B rcmake
without invoking
.BR cmake .
Complete target, compile, and link data come from CMake File API replies.
Without a File API reply, compile settings fall back to
.I compile_commands.json
and link data remain unavailable.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-preset " name"
Use the binary directory of configure preset
.IR name .
Pass this option twice to compare two presets, or mix it with one build
directory.
.TP
.BI \-S " source-dir"
Read presets from
.IR source-dir .
The default is the current working directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-only " sections"
Compare only a comma-separated list of sections chosen from
.BR targets ,
.BR compile ,
.BR link ,
.BR toolchain ,
.BR packages ,
and
.BR cache .
.TP
.BI \-\-config " a" "[:" b "]"
Compare one configuration in both trees, or configuration
.I a
in the first tree against configuration
.I b
in the second tree.
.TP
.BI \-\-target " name"
Compare only target
.IR name .
Repeat this option to include additional targets.
.TP
.BR \-\-cache " " key | all | none
Select which cache entries to compare.
The default is
.BR key .
.TP
.B \-\-no-normalize
Keep absolute paths instead of normalizing source and build roots.
.TP
.B \-\-prepare
Create the four stateless File API query files
.RB ( codemodel-v2 ,
.BR cache-v2 ,
.BR toolchains-v1 ,
and
.BR cmakeFiles-v1 )
under
.I .cmake/api/v1/query
in each listed build directory and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-json ", " \-\-color=auto | always | never ", " \-h ", " \-\-help
Emit one JSON diff report, control terminal color, or print usage.
.RE
.SS Formatter subcommand
.TP
.B rcmake fmt
Losslessly format
.I CMakeLists.txt
and
.I *.cmake
files using the concrete syntax representation.
Every edit modifies only whitespace and optional command identifier case, and
an independent verifier checks AST equivalence, protected tokens, and comment
attachment before writing.
Recursive discovery skips
.IR .git ,
.IR .hg ,
.IR .svn ,
.IR .bzr ,
.IR CMakeFiles ,
.IR Testing ,
nested build trees, AppleDouble
.I ._*
files, symbolic links, and any patterns configured in
.BR exclude .
In-place writes refuse to overwrite direct symbolic link operands.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Print paths of files that would change without writing to disk, and exit with
status 1 if any file needs formatting.
.TP
.B \-\-diff
Print unified diffs without writing to disk, and exit with status 1 if any file
needs formatting.
.TP
.B \-\-stdin
Read CMake input from standard input and write formatted bytes to standard
output.
Cannot be combined with path operands.
.TP
.BI \-\-stdin-filepath " path"
Associate a virtual file path with
.B \-\-stdin
so
.B rcmake fmt
resolves the nearest
.I \&.rcmake.toml
configuration for that directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show formatter usage and exit.
.PP
Formatting reads the nearest ancestor
.I \&.rcmake.toml
inside the project root.
Supported keys under
.B [fmt]
are
.B indent_width
(1 to 16, default 2),
.B line_width
(20 to 1000, default 100),
.B command_case
.RB ( preserve ,
.BR lower ,
or
.BR upper ),
.B end_of_line
.RB ( preserve ,
.BR lf ,
or
.BR crlf ).
Top-level
.B exclude
accepts an array of excluded path patterns shared with
.BR "rcmake lint" .
.RE
.SS Linter subcommand
.TP
.B rcmake lint
Run static analysis rules on
.I CMakeLists.txt
and
.I *.cmake
files.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-sarif
Write a SARIF 2.1.0 JSON report to standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-list-rules
Print all built-in rule identifiers, default severities, and descriptions and
exit.
.TP
.B \-\-deny-warnings
Treat warning findings as failures so
.B rcmake lint
exits with status 1 when any warning is reported.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show linter usage and exit.
.PP
The eight built-in rules and their default severities are
.B undefined-variable
(warning),
.B glob-without-configure-depends
(warning),
.B single-config-condition
(warning),
.B unguarded-build-type
(warning),
.B directory-options
(note),
.B obsolete-command
(warning),
.B old-policy
(warning),
and
.B fragile-if-expansion
(warning).
Configure rules in
.I \&.rcmake.toml
with top-level
.B exclude
(an array of excluded path patterns),
.B [lint]
.RB ( disable ),
and
.B [lint.severity]
(mapping a rule identifier to
.BR note ,
.BR warning ,
or
.BR error ).
Suppress a rule for a single command with a line comment of the form
.B "# rcmake-lint: disable=<rule>"
placed immediately before the command, inside its parentheses, or trailing on
its closing line.
Unknown or malformed directives report
.BR invalid-lint-directive .
.RE
.SS Verify subcommand
.TP
.B rcmake verify
Run both
.B rcmake
(in compatibility mode) and an upstream CMake 4.5.1 executable against
identical staged copies of a project, then compare configure status, File API
codemodel,
.IR CMakeCache.txt ,
.IR compile_commands.json ,
and Ninja dry-run output.
All upstream oracle execution stays isolated inside the sibling
.B rcmake-verify
companion binary so the core
.B rcmake
engine never runs upstream
.BR cmake .
Staging copies the source tree into a private scratch directory (skipping VCS
metadata and nested build trees) and never writes to the caller's source or
build directory.
Project configure scripts execute twice with the caller's permissions.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-oracle " cmake"
Path or executable name on
.B PATH
for the reference CMake 4.5.1 binary.
When omitted,
.B rcmake verify
uses
.B RCMAKE_ORACLE_CMAKE
if set.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " secs"
Overall wall-clock deadline in seconds for staging, both configures, and dry
runs.
Overrides
.B RCMAKE_VERIFY_TIMEOUT
(default 600).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write one machine-readable JSON report to standard output, including on
invalid-input exits.
.TP
.B \-\-
End
.B verify
options and pass the remaining configure arguments to both engines.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show verify usage and exit.
.RE
.SS Doctor subcommand
.TP
.BR "rcmake doctor" " [" \-B " " \fIbuild-dir\fP ]
Print the active
.B rcmake
version, persona,
.BR CMAKE_ROOT ,
probe cache location, mode, size, entry and blob counts, probe reuse warnings,
available compilers and build tools, and active
.B RCMAKE_*
environment variables.
When
.BI \-B " build-dir"
is given,
.B rcmake doctor
also inspects
.I CMakeCache.txt
and
.I CMakeFiles/rcmake/toolchain-inputs-v1.json
without running any compiler or project code, reporting missing tool files or
drift in
.BR CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE ,
.BR CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH ,
compiler binaries, or compiler launchers since the last successful native
configure.
.SS Cache subcommand
.TP
.B rcmake cache
Inspect, clear, export, or import the native compiler probe cache.
Set
.B RCMAKE_PROBE_CACHE_DIR
or
.B RCMAKE_CACHE_DIR
to select the storage root.
.RS
.TP
.B status
Show the cache directory, byte size, entry count, blob count, and staged import
candidate count.
This is the default action.
.TP
.B dir
Print the active probe cache directory.
.TP
.B clear
Remove cached probe entries, blobs, and staged import candidates.
.TP
.BI "export " file
Write valid probe entries and their blobs to a deterministic gzip tar archive
at
.I file
outside the cache root, run import validation on the archive before atomically
replacing
.IR file ,
and print its SHA-256 digest.
The archive contains compiler paths, compiler arguments, and captured compiler
output.
.TP
.BI "import " file " \fR[\fP\-\-sha256 " hex "\fR]\fP"
Validate the full archive before writing anything to the cache.
When
.BI \-\-sha256 " hex"
matches the 64-hex-digit archive digest from a trusted producer, entries and
blobs publish directly into the live probe cache without overwriting valid
local entries.
Without
.BR \-\-sha256 ,
entries are staged outside the live cache as untrusted candidates that never
trigger cache hits and can only repair missing blobs of matching local entries.
.RE
.SS Native configure options
Native extension flags that take a value use an equals sign in the same
argument.
.TP
.BR \-\-diagnostics=cmake | rich
Select diagnostic formatting.
.B cmake
matches upstream CMake 4.5.1 text, while
.B rich
renders source excerpts, spans, and suggested fixes.
When omitted in native mode,
.B rcmake
checks
.B RCMAKE_DIAGNOSTICS
and otherwise selects
.B rich
when standard error goes to a terminal and
.B cmake
when standard error is redirected.
Compatibility mode always uses
.BR cmake .
.TP
.BR \-\-profile [ =\fIdir\fP ]
Record configure timing and write
.IR trace.json ,
.IR stacks.folded ,
and an interactive
.I flamegraph.html
under
.IR dir ,
keeping per-run snapshots in
.IR dir/run-* .
When
.I dir
is omitted, output goes to
.I rcmake-profile
inside the build directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-hermetic [ =warn | strict ]
Audit undeclared configure inputs including environment variables, files outside
the source, build, and tool roots, subprocesses, and network access.
.B warn
is the default when no value is given, reporting violations and continuing.
.B strict
rejects undeclared inputs with a non-zero exit status.
Configure allowlists with
.BR RCMAKE_HERMETIC_ALLOW_ENV ,
.BR RCMAKE_HERMETIC_ALLOW_PATHS ,
and
.BR RCMAKE_HERMETIC_ALLOW_PROGRAMS .
.TP
.BR \-\-fetch-lock=off | auto | update | frozen
Control FetchContent lockfile verification and pinned source reuse.
.B off
disables lockfile checks.
.B auto
is the default and verifies against an existing lockfile when present.
.B update
records resolved archive and Git pins into the lockfile.
.B frozen
requires every fetched dependency to match a verified pin and blocks unpinned
or unsupported transfers.
.TP
.B \-\-no-probe-cache
Disable the persistent compiler probe cache for this configure run.
To select a custom shared cache root or probe cache root, set
.B RCMAKE_CACHE_DIR
or
.B RCMAKE_PROBE_CACHE_DIR
in the environment.
.TP
.B \-\-export-compile-commands
Enable
.B CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS=ON
for this configure run.
In native mode with a multi-configuration generator
.RB ( "Ninja Multi-Config" ,
.BR Xcode ,
or
.BR "Visual Studio" ),
.B rcmake
publishes per-configuration
.I compile_commands_<Config>.json
files alongside a root
.I compile_commands.json
for the default configuration and tracks owned files in
.IR CMakeFiles/rcmake/compile-commands-v1.json .
.SH CONFIGURE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-S " path-to-source"
Explicitly specify the source directory.
.TP
.BI \-B " path-to-build"
Explicitly specify the build directory.
.TP
.BI \-C " initial-cache"
Preload a script to populate the cache before configuring.
.TP
.BI \-D " var" "[:" type "]=" value
Create or update a CMake cache entry.
.TP
.BI \-U " globbing-expr"
Remove matching entries from the CMake cache.
.TP
.BI \-G " generator-name"
Select a build system generator.
Supported generators are
.BR "Unix Makefiles" ,
.BR Ninja ,
.BR "Ninja Multi-Config" ,
.B Xcode
on macOS,
.B "Visual Studio 17 2022"
on Windows, and
.B "Visual Studio 18 2026"
on Windows.
.TP
.BI \-T " toolset-name"
Specify the generator toolset where supported.
.TP
.BI \-A " platform-name"
Specify the generator platform where supported.
.TP
.BI \-\-toolchain " file"
Specify a toolchain file
.RB ( CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE ).
.TP
.BI \-\-install-prefix " dir"
Specify the installation prefix
.RB ( CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX ).
.TP
.BI \-\-project-file " name"
Specify an alternate top-level project listfile name.
.TP
.BI \-\-preset " name"
Use a configure preset from
.I CMakePresets.json
or
.IR CMakeUserPresets.json .
.TP
.BI \-\-presets-file " file"
Read presets from a specific file.
.TP
.BR \-\-list-presets [ =\fItype\fP ]
List available or defined presets.
Valid types are
.BR configure ,
.BR build ,
.BR test ,
.BR package ,
.BR workflow ,
.BR all ,
.BR defined ,
and any type suffixed with
.BR \-defined .
.TP
.B \-\-fresh
Remove any existing cache file before configuring.
.TP
.BI \-W category "\fR, \fP" \-Wno- category "\fR, \fP" \-Werror= category "\fR, \fP" \-Wno-error= category
Enable, suppress, or promote diagnostic warning categories
.RB ( dev ,
.BR author ,
.BR deprecated ,
.BR policy ,
.BR strict ,
.BR experimental ,
.BR non-target-directive ,
.BR install-absolute-destination ,
.BR uninitialized ,
.BR unused-cli ).
.TP
.BR \-\-warn-uninitialized ", " \-\-no-warn-unused-cli ", " \-\-check-system-vars
Control uninitialized variable, unused CLI variable, and system file checks.
.TP
.BR \-\-compile-no-warning-as-error ", " \-\-link-no-warning-as-error
Ignore
.B COMPILE_WARNING_AS_ERROR
or
.B LINK_WARNING_AS_ERROR
properties and variables.
.TP
.BR \-\-log-level= ERROR|WARNING|NOTICE|STATUS|VERBOSE|DEBUG|TRACE
Set message verbosity.
.B \-\-log-context
prepends message context.
.TP
.BR \-\-trace ", " \-\-trace-expand ", " \-\-trace-format=human|json-v1 ", " \-\-trace-source=\fIfile\fP ", " \-\-trace-redirect=\fIfile\fP
Enable CMake script tracing and control trace output.
.TP
.BR \-\-debug-output ", " \-\-debug-trycompile ", " \-\-debug-find ", " \-\-debug-find-pkg=\fIpkgs\fP ", " \-\-debug-find-var=\fIvars\fP
Enable configure and find-command debug diagnostics.
.TP
.BR \-\-debugger ", " \-\-debugger-pipe=\fIpath\fP ", " \-\-debugger-dap-log=\fIfile\fP
Start the CMake 4.5.1 Debug Adapter Protocol server for a configure or
.B \-P
script run over a Unix domain socket at
.I path
on macOS and Linux, optionally recording DAP traffic to
.IR file .
Windows named-pipe transport is not yet supported in
.BR "rcmake 0.2.1" .
.TP
.BI \-\-sarif-output= file
Write SARIF 2.1.0 diagnostic output to
.IR file .
.TP
.BI \-\-graphviz= file
Generate a Graphviz dependency graph.
.TP
.BR \-\-profiling-format=google-trace ", " \-\-profiling-output=\fIfile\fP
Write CMake-format Google Trace profiling JSON.
.TP
.BR \-L [ A ][ H ] ", " \-LR [ A ][ H ] " " \fIregex\fP
List cached variables, optionally including advanced entries, help strings,
or regex filtering.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-P " " \fIfile\fP ", " \-E " " \fIcmd\fP ", " \-\-open " " \fIdir\fP ", " \-\-find-package ", " \-\-system-information " [" \fIfile\fP "], " \-\-print-config-dir
Run view mode, script mode, cross-platform command mode, open a generated
project, run legacy find-package mode, dump system information, or print the
user File API config directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-H ", " \-\-help ", " \-\-version [ =json-v1 ] ", " \-\-help-*
Print usage, version information
.RB ( "cmake version 4.5.1"
and
.BR "rcmake 0.2.1" ),
or bundled CMake 4.5.1 reference topics
.RB ( \-\-help-command ,
.BR \-\-help-diagnostic ,
.BR \-\-help-manual ,
.BR \-\-help-module ,
.BR \-\-help-policy ,
.BR \-\-help-property ,
.BR \-\-help-variable ,
and their
.B \-list
variants).
.SH BUILD, INSTALL, AND WORKFLOW MODES
.TP
.BI "\-\-build " dir
Build a generated project tree.
Accepts
.BR \-\-preset ,
.BR \-\-presets-file ,
.BR \-\-list-presets [ =defined ],
.BR \-j ", " \-\-parallel
.RI [ jobs ],
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target
.IR tgt ,
.BR \-\-config
.IR cfg ,
.BR \-\-clean-first ,
.BR \-\-resolve-package-references=on|only|off ,
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose ,
and
.B \-\-
followed by native build tool arguments.
.TP
.BI "\-\-install " dir
Install a generated project tree.
Accepts
.BR \-\-config
.IR cfg ,
.BR \-\-component
.IR comp ,
.BR \-\-default-directory-permissions
.IR perm ,
.BR \-j ", " \-\-parallel
.IR jobs ,
.BR \-\-prefix
.IR dir ,
.BR \-\-strip ,
and
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose .
.TP
.B \-\-workflow
Run a workflow preset's configure, build, test, and package steps.
Accepts
.BR \-\-preset ,
.BR \-\-presets-file ,
.BR \-\-list-presets [ =defined ],
and
.BR \-\-fresh .
.SH COMPANION TOOLS
.SS ccmake
Started through the
.B ccmake
symlink or as
.B "rcmake ccmake"
on Unix (macOS and Linux), the binary runs a clean-room Rust interactive
terminal cache editor with distinct configure and generate phases, captured
child output, and no
.B ncurses
dependency.
See
.BR ccmake (1)
for options and interactive key bindings.
Windows is not yet supported in
.BR "rcmake 0.2.1" .
.SS ctest
When started through a
.B ctest
symlink in compatibility mode or as
.BR "rcmake ctest" ,
the binary runs CMake test suites with parallel scheduling, GNU make jobserver
access, fixtures, resource specifications, labels, repeat modes, JUnit XML,
dashboard submission, and
.B \-S
scripts.
Common options include
.BR \-\-test-dir
.IR dir ,
.BR \-C
.IR cfg ,
.BR \-R
.I regex
to include tests,
.BR \-E
.I regex
to exclude tests,
.BR \-L
.I regex
to include labels,
.BR \-LE
.I regex
to exclude labels,
.BR \-j ", " \-\-parallel
.RI [ jobs ],
.BR \-\-output-on-failure ,
.BR \-\-output-junit
.IR file ,
.BR \-\-preset
.IR name ,
.BR \-\-rerun-failed ,
.BR \-\-stop-on-failure ,
.BR \-\-repeat
.IR mode:n ,
.BR \-\-timeout
.IR secs ,
.BR \-N ", " \-\-show-only [ =human|json-v1|json-v1-raw ],
.BR \-V ", " \-VV ", " \-Q ,
and
.BR \-S
.IR script .
.SS cpack
When started through a
.B cpack
symlink in compatibility mode or as
.BR "rcmake cpack" ,
the binary packages build artifacts using
.BR \-G
.I generators
.RB ( TGZ ,
.BR TXZ ,
.BR TZST ,
.BR TBZ2 ,
.BR TZ ,
.BR TAR ,
.BR STGZ ,
.BR ZIP ,
.BR 7Z ,
their compression variants, Linux
.B DEB
and
.BR RPM ,
.BR External ,
macOS
.BR Bundle ,
.BR DragNDrop ,
and
.BR productbuild ,
Windows
.B WIX
supporting WiX v3 and v4, and cross-platform
.BR NSIS ,
.BR NSIS64 ,
and
.BR IFW ),
.BR \-C
.IR configs ,
.BR \-D
.IR var=value ,
.BR \-\-config
.IR file ,
.BR \-P
.IR name ,
.BR \-R
.IR version ,
.BR \-B
.IR dir ,
.BR \-\-vendor
.IR name ,
.BR \-\-preset
.IR name ,
.BR \-\-presets-file
.IR file ,
.BR \-\-list-presets ,
.BR \-V ", " \-\-verbose ,
.BR \-\-debug ,
.BR \-\-trace ,
and
.BR \-\-trace-expand .
.SS rcmake-lsp
Started through the
.B rcmake-lsp
symlink or as
.BR "rcmake lsp" ,
the same multi-call binary runs a Language Server Protocol server for
.I CMakeLists.txt
and
.I *.cmake
files over standard input and standard output using JSON-RPC
.B Content-Length
framing.
It accepts
.BR \-h ,
.BR \-\-help ,
.BR \-V ,
.BR \-\-version ,
.BR \-\-stdio ,
and
.BI \-\-clientProcessId= pid .
It provides hover, completion, go to definition, document symbols, semantic
tokens, quick fixes, lossless
.I \&.rcmake.toml
formatting, all eight static
.B rcmake lint
rules (watching
.I \&.rcmake.toml
and included project files), and bounded in-memory evaluated diagnostics.
When built with the
.B eval,stdio
features, which release archives enable by default, hover and diagnostics also
reflect evaluated variables, targets, and generator expressions without
spawning external processes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Command-line options take precedence over environment variables.
Native speed and diagnostic variables apply only in native
.B rcmake
mode.
.SS Mode and output
.TP
.B RCMAKE_ORACLE_MODE
Set to
.B 1
to force compatibility mode even when invoked as
.BR rcmake .
.TP
.B RCMAKE_DIAGNOSTICS
Set to
.B cmake
or
.B rich
in native mode.
When unset,
.B rcmake
defaults to
.B rich
on a terminal standard error and
.B cmake
otherwise.
.TP
.BR NO_COLOR ", " CLICOLOR_FORCE
Disable ANSI color when
.B NO_COLOR
is non-empty.
.B CLICOLOR_FORCE=1
forces ANSI color in rich mode and overrides
.BR NO_COLOR .
.TP
.B RCMAKE_PROFILE
Set the native configure profile output directory.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_NO_HINTS
Set to
.B 1
to suppress trailing
.B find_package()
hint lines on standard error after failed package lookups in native mode.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_EXEC_LOG
Write JSON Lines invocation records containing the
.B tool
and effective
.B persona
fields to this path.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_VENDORED_DATA_ROOT
Override the directory containing bundled CMake 4.5.1
.IR Modules/ ,
.IR Templates/ ,
and
.I Help/
files.
.SS Probe cache and incremental replay
.TP
.B RCMAKE_CACHE_DIR
Override the shared storage root for the compiler probe cache and FetchContent
cache.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_CACHE_MAX_SIZE
Set the shared store size limit in bytes.
The default is 2 GiB.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_PROBE_CACHE
Select
.B readwrite
as the default, or select
.BR readonly ,
.BR verify ,
or
.BR off .
.TP
.B RCMAKE_NO_PROBE_CACHE
Set to
.B 1
to disable the probe cache.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_PROBE_CACHE_DIR
Override the probe storage root separately from
.BR RCMAKE_CACHE_DIR .
.TP
.B RCMAKE_PROBE_JOBS
Set a positive integer number of concurrent probe jobs.
The default is the smaller of 4 and the logical CPU count.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_NO_INCREMENTAL
Set to
.B 1
to disable incremental configure replay.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_REPLAY_SETUP
Set to
.B 0
to disable incremental configure replay when toolchain files, configure
presets,
.B \-C
scripts, or
.I PreLoad.cmake
files are present.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_OFFLINE
Set to
.B 1
to disable remote probe cache access.
.TP
.BR RCMAKE_CACHE_REMOTE ", " RCMAKE_CACHE_REMOTE_AUTH ", " RCMAKE_CACHE_REMOTE_TOKEN ", " RCMAKE_CACHE_REMOTE_HEADER ", " RCMAKE_CACHE_REMOTE_WRITE ", " RCMAKE_CACHE_REMOTE_EXPORT_CAPTURED_OUTPUT ", " RCMAKE_CACHE_REMOTE_EXPORT_TIMEOUT ", " RCMAKE_CACHE_REMOTE_CURL
Configure an optional HTTPS remote probe cache supporting
.BR anonymous ,
.BR bearer ,
.BR header ,
or
.B s3
authentication.
.SS FetchContent, hermetic checks, verify, and CPack
.TP
.B RCMAKE_FETCH_LOCK
Select
.B auto
as the default, or select
.BR off ,
.BR update ,
or
.BR frozen .
.TP
.B RCMAKE_FETCH_LOCK_FILE
Override the lockfile path.
The default is
.I rcmake-fetch.lock
in the source directory.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_FETCH_OFFLINE
Set to
.B 1
to disable network transfers for FetchContent and ExternalProject.
.TP
.BR RCMAKE_FETCH_PREFETCH ", " RCMAKE_FETCH_JOBS ", " RCMAKE_FETCH_GIT_READ_ONLY ", " RCMAKE_FETCH_GIT_MAX_SIZE
Control parallel FetchContent prefetching and Git mirror cache limits.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_HERMETIC
Select
.B off
as the default, or select
.BR warn ,
or
.BR strict .
.TP
.BR RCMAKE_HERMETIC_ALLOW_ENV ", " RCMAKE_HERMETIC_ALLOW_PATHS ", " RCMAKE_HERMETIC_ALLOW_PROGRAMS
Set semicolon-separated allowlists of environment variable names, absolute
directory or file paths, and absolute executable paths permitted in hermetic
mode.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_EXTRACT_MAX_BYTES
Override the archive extraction output size limit in bytes (clamped to the
64 GiB ceiling).
.TP
.B RCMAKE_ORACLE_CMAKE
Default reference CMake 4.5.1 executable path used by
.B rcmake verify
when
.B \-\-oracle
is omitted, and by
.B rcmake-harness
differential suites.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_VERIFY_TIMEOUT
Default wall-clock timeout in seconds for
.B rcmake verify
(default 600).
Overridden by
.BR \-\-timeout .
.TP
.B RCMAKE_CPACK_TOOL_TIMEOUT
Optional timeout in seconds for external CPack installer tools such as
.BR makensis ,
.BR wix ,
.BR pkgbuild ,
.BR productbuild ,
and
.BR binarycreator .
.SS Standard CMake and CTest variables
.TP
.BR CMAKE_GENERATOR ", " CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH ", " CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL ", " CMAKE_INSTALL_PARALLEL_LEVEL ", " CTEST_PARALLEL_LEVEL ", " CTEST_OUTPUT_ON_FAILURE
Standard CMake and CTest variables honored by
.BR rcmake ,
.BR cmake ,
and
.BR ctest .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command succeeded.
For
.BR "rcmake explain" ,
the requested target, variable, package, or generator expression succeeded.
For
.BR "rcmake diff-config" ,
no differences were found and all requested sections had complete evidence.
For
.BR "rcmake fmt" ,
all files are formatted.
For
.BR "rcmake lint" ,
no error findings (and with
.BR \-\-deny-warnings ,
no warning findings) were reported.
For
.BR "rcmake verify" ,
all applicable sections matched CMake 4.5.1.
For
.BR "rcmake doctor" ,
the environment and optional build directory are clean.
.TP
.B 1
Configure, generation, build, install, test, or packaging failed.
For
.BR "rcmake explain" ,
the requested target, variable, package, or typed filter was missing, ambiguous,
or unmatched, or evaluation failed or remained provisional.
For
.B rcmake diff-config
and
.BR "rcmake verify" ,
differences were observed.
For
.B "rcmake fmt \-\-check"
and
.BR \-\-diff ,
at least one file needs formatting.
For
.BR "rcmake lint" ,
error findings (or warning findings with
.BR \-\-deny-warnings )
were reported.
For
.BR "rcmake doctor \-B" ,
the cache or receipt is missing, unreadable, or shows missing tools or
toolchain drift.
For
.BR "rcmake cache" ,
a store, archive, or digest error occurred.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments to native subcommands
.RB ( explain ,
.BR diff-config ,
.BR fmt ,
.BR lint ,
.BR verify ,
.BR doctor ,
.BR cache ,
or
.BR rcmake-lsp ),
an unavailable configured build directory, incomplete section evidence in
.B diff-config
or
.BR "explain \-\-find" ,
configuration, parse, file system, symlink overwrite refusal, or resource budget
errors in
.B fmt
and
.BR lint ,
or a missing
.B rcmake-verify
companion, invalid oracle, matched failure, or incomplete evidence in
.BR "rcmake verify" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <prefix>/share/cmake-4.5/
Bundled CMake 4.5.1 modules, templates, and compressed help reference installed
next to
.IR <prefix>/bin/rcmake .
.TP
.I \&.rcmake.toml
Project formatter and linter configuration file discovered by walking upward to
the project root.
.TP
.I CMakeCache.txt
Generated build-tree cache read by
.BR "rcmake explain" ,
.BR "rcmake diff-config" ,
.BR "rcmake doctor" ,
and incremental reconfigures.
.TP
.IR CMakePresets.json ", " CMakeUserPresets.json
Project and user CMake Presets files using schema version 13.
.TP
.I rcmake-fetch.lock
Default FetchContent lockfile in the project source directory.
.TP
.I <build>/CMakeFiles/rcmake/configure.v1.bin
Native incremental configure replay manifest.
.TP
.I <build>/CMakeFiles/rcmake/find-trace.v1.json
Saved native
.B find_package()
search trace read by
.B rcmake explain \-\-find
and
.BR "rcmake diff-config" .
.TP
.I <build>/CMakeFiles/rcmake/toolchain-inputs-v1.json
Native toolchain, compiler, launcher, and prefix drift receipt read by warm
reconfigures and
.BR "rcmake doctor \-B" .
.TP
.I <build>/CMakeFiles/rcmake/compile-commands-v1.json
Ownership manifest for native multi-configuration
.I compile_commands_<Config>.json
files.
.TP
.I <build>/rcmake-profile/
Default output directory for
.B \-\-profile
containing
.IR trace.json ,
.IR stacks.folded ,
.IR flamegraph.html ,
and per-run directories under
.IR run-* .
.TP
.I ~/Library/Caches/rcmake
Default cache directory on macOS.
On Linux the default is
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/rcmake
or
.IR ~/.cache/rcmake .
On Windows the default is
.IR %LOCALAPPDATA%\ercmake\ecache .
.B RCMAKE_CACHE_DIR
and
.B RCMAKE_PROBE_CACHE_DIR
override this location.
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure and build a project with Ninja and export multi-configuration compile
databases.
.PP
.EX
rcmake -S . -B build -G "Ninja Multi-Config" --export-compile-commands
rcmake --build build --config Release
.EE
.PP
Explain where target
.B app
gets its
.B \-O2
flag, trace a dependency path, inspect a failed package lookup, or evaluate a
generator expression.
.PP
.EX
rcmake explain app -B build --flag -O2
rcmake explain app -B build --dep zlib --config Release
rcmake explain why-not Boost -B build
rcmake explain --eval '$<$<CONFIG:Debug>:-DTRACE>' -B build --config Debug
.EE
.PP
Compare two build directories, check formatting, and run the static linter in
CI.
.PP
.EX
rcmake diff-config build-main build-pr --only compile,link
rcmake fmt --check
rcmake lint --deny-warnings --sarif > rcmake-lint.sarif
.EE
.PP
Verify configure parity against CMake 4.5.1, check build-tree drift, and share
a portable probe cache archive.
.PP
.EX
rcmake verify --oracle /path/to/cmake-4.5.1 -- -S . -G Ninja
rcmake doctor -B build
rcmake cache export probes.tar.gz
rcmake cache import probes.tar.gz --sha256 <64-hex-digest>
.EE
.PP
Debug a configure script over a Unix domain socket or launch the interactive
cache editor.
.PP
.EX
rcmake -S . -B build --debugger --debugger-pipe=/tmp/cmake-dap.sock
ccmake -B build
.EE
.PP
Run tests through the compatibility alias.
.PP
.EX
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure -j
.EE
